# Bokeh JS/Python version sync

The SPA bundles **stock** **`@bokeh/bokehjs`** from npm (no `patch-package` vendor overrides). Embed timing mitigations live in app code: **`patch-resize-observer-for-bokeh.js`**, **`BokehEmbed`** viewport gating, and post-`Document.idle` settle (see **`bokeh-layout-surface-split.mdc`**).

If Bokeh regressions reappear in the browser console after upgrades, prefer fixing **`json_item`** contracts / React embed timing first; reintroducing a **`patch-package`** patch is a last resort (document why and keep **`postinstall`** + `patches/` in sync).

## Single-version sync (one table)

| Location | What to sync |
|----------|----------------|
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/package.json` | `@bokeh/bokehjs` exact version |
| `pyproject.toml` | `bokeh==X.Y.Z` (Python `json_item` / figures must match JS embed major.minor.patch policy) |
| `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/job_plot_artifacts.py` | Fingerprint includes `bokeh.__version__` — expect artifact churn / cache behavior on bump |
| `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/tests/test_bokeh_job_list_embed_browser_e2e.py` | `_BOKEH_CDN_JS` jsDelivr pin for `@bokeh/bokehjs@X.Y.Z` |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/test-fixtures/bokeh-*.json` | Regenerate if serialized `json_item` / doc schema changes (per `web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`) |
| `hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/bokehInit.js` / `patch-resize-observer-for-bokeh.js` | Re-validate embed + ResizeObserver behavior after Bokeh upgrades |

## Workflow (bump checklist)

1. Bump **`@bokeh/bokehjs`** and **`bokeh==…`** together per the table above.
2. `cd hpcperfstats/site/frontend && npm ci` (or `npm install`).
3. `npm run build` → fix bundle/import breaks (SPA-only; default build does not emit **`bokeh-playwright-smoke.html`**).
4. `npm test -- --run` (Vitest), including Bokeh embed tests as needed.
5. `pytest hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/tests/test_bokeh_job_list_embed_browser_e2e.py` (Playwright + CDN Bokeh; see below). For the **third** (Vite-bundle) test, run **`npm run build:with-bokeh-playwright-smoke`** first or that test skips.
6. Regenerate **`test-fixtures`** if schema changes; update **`docs/TESTING.md`** if workflow or commands change (`testing-doc-sync.mdc`).

## Playwright vs production bundle

`test_bokeh_job_list_embed_browser_e2e.py` loads Bokeh from **jsDelivr** at the same **version** as `package.json` for two tests, and a third starts **`vite preview`** against the built tree so **`bokeh-playwright-smoke.html`** exercises the **same Vite chunk graph** as production (requires **`npm run build:with-bokeh-playwright-smoke`** in `hpcperfstats/site/frontend`, or **`BUILD_BOKEH_SMOKE=1 npm run build`**; default **`npm run build`** is SPA-only—or the third test skips). After Bokeh bumps, spot-check real pages (job list distributions, job detail plots) for console cleanliness if Vitest/Playwright are green.

## Overlap

- **`job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc`** — fingerprints and artifact invalidation on Bokeh version changes.
- **`no-cdn-in-production.mdc`** — CDN only where explicitly test-only; production uses the bundled library.
- **`web-pages-e2e-test-maintenance.mdc`** — fixtures, `_BOKEH_CDN_JS`, and regeneration steps.
- **`bokeh-layout-surface-split.mdc`** — embed layout, `BokehEmbed`, ResizeObserver patch.
- **`testing-doc-sync.mdc`** — keep `docs/TESTING.md` aligned with npm commands.
